including recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-10-12T12:01:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 121201 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 601 AM MDT Mon Oct 12 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Unseasonably warm and mostly dry conditions will persist across the forecast area today before cooler temperatures arrive Tuesday. - Isolated showers remain possible for the northern mountains through Monday, before precipitation chances increase and sprea","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-10-12T08:34:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today through Friday... A few light showers have been observed over the Park Range early this morning as well as a few sprinkles mainly west of the Continental Divide. Shower chances will decrease over the next few hours with mostly sunny skies and dry weather expected for the day. Winds are currently lighter than they were a couple hours ago, with sporadic gusts only reaching about ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"hyd01","station_name":"Hayden","distance_km":30.9,"soil_temp_5cm_f":54.93,"soil_temp_15cm_